  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Astral Elf Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Astral Elf is yet another extraplanar elf, joining the Eladrin and the Shadar-Kai in the “we can teleport” club. They also add some extra proficiencies and a just a splash of spellcasting to produce an interesting, versatile race that’s a good basis for many builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Notably different from other elves published in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Monsters of the Multiverse",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/motm/fantastical-races#AirGenasiTraits"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and later supplements, the Astral Elf’s version of Trance allows them to pick proficiencies in one skill and one tool rather than two weapons or tools. While this limits weapon options (which are helpful for a handful of builds, especially for monks and rogues), an additional skill is often much more valuable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While they lack a clear niche, the versatility of the Astral Elf’s traits makes them easy to use with nearly any class. You won’t excel at anything in particular, but you can build almost anything and find a way to make the Astral Elf’s traits interesting."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
